From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Market Canopy <office@marketcanopy.invalid>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Sign in to Market Canopy from the start screen

The start screen's Cloud item (where upstream has Clouds) shows the
Market Canopy account the native account module keeps (desktop-sdk patch
0002), laid out like upstream's available clouds: one row for each
organization the person belongs to, with its logo (the organization's
own, else upstream's generic cloud), its name and Connect. Signed
out, one Market Canopy row offers Sign in, which opens the system
browser; signing in, Update required and offline say so on the page.
Signing out is the web page's, whose sign-out reaches the module through
portal:logout. Market Canopy's cloud connection is made by native code
after sign-in, so there is no connect step: Connect selects the
organization when it is not the active one, then opens a tab on the
provider's startPage (providers/marketcanopy, P07), which the module
connects before the page shows the drive. Window focus asks the module
to read the credential store again (P02 contract 5.4), whichever page
shows.

Both shells hand every launch argument and opened link to the module
first (CallCommand "mc:scheme:"), so a sign-in callback forwarded by the
single-instance check, or a link that carries a credential, is never
opened as a document.
